 "text": "Buying a laptop soon? AI's making it pricier. Well, AI's making it pricier. Well, AI data centers are. Which is backwards. Laptops get better for the same money, usually right after you buy one. But this past year, in the US, computers went up almost 10%. Mostly because your laptop runs on memory chips, and so do AI data centers by the mountain. They pay more, so they get first dibs. Which means what's left costs about five times last year's price, and laptop makers pass that on. Normally, you'd wait for the better one. But chip makers say next year's even tighter. So that's how an AI data center ends up on your next laptop's price tag.",
